Hrrmm, my imagination doesn't kick in at all when I'm playing Nethack.  
Maybe it's too abstract to me.  I don't even think of the enemies as 
monsters, just letters, and some letters are harder than others.  Way back 
when I played tile version I think the simple pictures of what the monsters 
looked like fed my imagination a lot better.  It actually seemed like I was 
in a dungeon.  With ASCII Nethack, it just feels like I'm playing an 
incredibly fun text editor.  It's a great game, don't get me wrong, but 
with the ASCII interface it just doesn't give me the same immersiveness 
that any other game with graphics does.

Although I recently played some AD&D in an IRC channel and I was vividly 
imagining the surroundings, even though there were no graphics involved.  
And I do vividly imagine stuff when I'm reading books too.  Maybe at some 
time I used to do this with Nethack; I no longer remember.  All I know is 
I'm long past the imagining stage with Nethack and it's all about the 
numbers.

